# The users this broker authenticates.
#
# Loaded with --aclfile, and mounted read-only: ACL SETUSER during a test
# changes memory only, so nothing a test creates survives a restart and no
# test can rewrite this file by calling ACL SAVE.

# Off, and deliberately not merely passworded. Something has to refuse an
# anonymous connection, or the driver's rejected-credentials path has nothing
# to report and the degraded state it produces cannot be asserted.
user default off

# What the app and the live tests connect as.
user mqstudio on >mqstudio ~* &* +@all

# A user with real restrictions, so the ACL board has a rule worth drawing.
# With every user holding +@all the key-pattern and command-rule columns would
# be constants, and a page that renders the same string for every row proves
# nothing about whether it read the broker.
user mqs-seed-readonly on >readonly ~mqs-seed:* &* +@read +@connection
